11
00:47:51,000 --> 00:47:57,000
Believe Me: The Abduction of Lisa McVey is a 2018 American true
crime film, filmed in Canada, directed by Jim Donovan.

12
00:52:12,000 --> 00:52:18,000
The film was released on September 30, 2018, by Lifetime in
United States  and by Showcase in Canada.

13
00:56:33,000 --> 00:56:39,000
On June 4, 2021, it was released worldwide by Netflix.

14
01:00:54,000 --> 01:01:00,000
The film stars Katie Douglas, Rossif Sutherland, and David James Elliott.

15
01:05:15,000 --> 01:05:21,000
The film recounts the true story of Lisa McVey who was abducted and
raped for 26 hours by serial killer Bobby Joe Long in 1984.

16
01:09:36,000 --> 01:09:42,000
In addition to its television broadcast, the film also received a special theatrical screening
in Tampa, at the very same theater where Bobby Joe Long was arrested in 1984.

17
01:13:57,000 --> 01:14:03,000
The screening of this movie was attended by the real Lisa McVey Noland.

18
01:18:18,000 --> 01:18:24,000
The film explores themes of suicide, sexual abuse,
kidnapping, detective, based on true story.

19
01:22:39,000 --> 01:22:45,000
The tone is emotional.
